## 6. How to read the result

When a log entry appears, focus on these parts:

* **Resource section**
  Confirms the endpoint identity through `resource_container`, `location`, and `endpoint_id`.

* **Timestamp**
  Confirms when the request or container event occurred.

* **Severity**
  Helps distinguish debug/info output from errors.

* **Message body**
  Shows stdout/stderr output or access-log details.

* **Project selection**
  Confirms you are looking at the correct unified project.

---

## 7. Notes and gotchas

* **Access logging is disabled by default** for online inference endpoints, so if you do not see per-request logs, the feature may not have been enabled.
* **Container logging behavior differs by endpoint version**: enabled by default on `v1`, disabled by default on `v1beta1`.
* **Request-response logging is BigQuery-based**, so it is not part of Logs Explorer validation.
* **Model Garden metrics and logs are not the same thing**: the metrics use `PublisherModel`, while Logs Explorer validation is centered on the deployed `Endpoint` resource. ([docs.cloud.google.com](https://docs.cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/docs/predictions/online-prediction-logging?utm_source=chatgpt.com) [docs.cloud.google.com](https://docs.cloud.google.com/monitoring/api/resources?utm_source=chatgpt.com))

